    "q-73412": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73412",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "${(7y)}^{1/4}=$",
      "worked_solution": "In general, the fractional exponent ${x}^{1/n}$ can also be written as the $n$th root $\\sqrt[n]{x}.$ In this particular case, $n=4,$ $x=7y,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n{(7y)}^{1/4}=\\sqrt[4]{7y}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
