      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${q}^{1/3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "In general, the fractional exponent ${x}^{1/n}$ can also be written as the $n$th root $\\sqrt[n]{x}.$ In this particular case, $n=3,$ $x=q,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n{q}^{1/3}=\\sqrt[3]{q}\n$$",
