      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Express $\\sqrt[5]{7a}$ using power notation.",
      "worked_solution": "In general, the $n$th root $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can also be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$ In this particular case, $n=5,$ $x=7a,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[5]{7a}={(7a)}^{1/5}\n$$",
