    "q-51484": {
      "dom_id": "step-q51484",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Express ${v}^{-1/3}$ using radical notation.",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that in general, a negative exponent can be converted to a positive exponent if we take the reciprocal. Here, we have:\n\n$$\n{v}^{-1/3}=\\frac{1}{{v}^{1/3}}\n$$\n\nNow, we can proceed as usual to convert the fractional exponent to a radical:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{v}^{1/3}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{v}}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n{v}^{-1/3}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{v}}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-51484-a",
