    "q-72813": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72813",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$(9v)^{-1/4}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that in general, a negative exponent can be converted to a positive exponent if we take the reciprocal. Here, we have:\n\n$$\n(9v)^{-1/4}=\\frac{1}{(9v)^{1/4}}\n$$\n\nNow, we can proceed as usual to convert the fractional exponent to a radical:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{(9v)^{1/4}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{9v}}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n(9v)^{-1/4}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{9v}}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-72813-a",
