    "q-72819": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72819",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Write $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[9]{t}}$ using power notation.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert the radical to a fractional exponent:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[9]{t}}=\\frac{1}{{t}^{1/9}}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we take the reciprocal and convert the exponent to a negative exponent:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{t}^{1/9}}={t}^{-1/9}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[9]{t}}={t}^{-1/9}\n$$",
